This is a TanStack Start app with a Convex backend. Use Bun for package
management, scripts, and one-off CLIs.

# Commands

- Install dependencies with `bun install`.
- Run scripts with `bun --bun run <script>`.
- Use `bunx --bun` for CLIs, for example:
  - `bunx --bun convex dev`
  - `bunx --bun convex codegen`
  - `bunx --bun convex ai-files install`
  - `bunx --bun shadcn@latest add button`
- Avoid `npm`, `pnpm`, and `npx` unless a tool has no Bun-compatible path.

# TanStack Start

- Routes live in `src/routes`.
- Do not edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts` manually.
- Keep framework code on Vite-era TanStack Start APIs:
  - `@tanstack/react-start`
  - `vite.config.ts`
  - `createServerFileRoute(...).methods(...)` for server file routes when
    needed
- Do not introduce legacy Vinxi or `@tanstack/start` patterns.

# Convex

- Before editing Convex code, read `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md`.
- Convex generated files under `convex/_generated` are tool-owned.
- Use `bunx --bun convex codegen` after Convex API or schema changes.
- Use `bunx --bun convex ai-files install` to refresh Convex AI guidance.

# Environment

- Client-exposed environment variables must start with `VITE_`.
- Keep `.env.example` and `src/env.ts` synchronized.
- Prefer importing from `src/env.ts` over reading `(import.meta as any).env`
  directly in app code.
